<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Travel and Expense Policy — effective January 1, 2026 — accessible alternative</title>
  <style>body{font:18px/1.6 Georgia,serif;max-width:72ch;margin:0 auto;padding:2rem;color:#171717;background:#fff}h1,h2{font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:1.2}.notice{border-left:.35rem solid #24557a;padding:.75rem 1rem;background:#eef6fb}a:focus{outline:3px solid #c45500;outline-offset:3px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f5f5f5;background:#171717}.notice{background:#163247}}</style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <h1>Travel and Expense Policy — effective January 1, 2026</h1>
    <p class="notice"><strong>Training notice:</strong> Fictional training data — not for operational use</p>
    <section aria-labelledby="s1"><h2 id="s1">Core requirements</h2><p>Receipts are required for expenses of $25 or more. Business purpose is required for every expense. The employee may not approve their own expense.</p></section>
<section aria-labelledby="s2"><h2 id="s2">Limits</h2><p>Domestic hotel limit is $275 per night before tax. Meals are limited to $90 per person per day. Airfare must be economy class unless the CFO pre-approves another class in writing. Alcohol is reimbursable only when itemized and associated with an approved client event.</p></section>
<section aria-labelledby="s3"><h2 id="s3">Timing and exceptions</h2><p>Expense reports must be submitted within 30 days after the transaction. Documented exceptions require Finance Director approval.</p></section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
